; ZipMax language file: English (built-in default)
; Encoding: UTF-8.  Format:  KEY = "text"   (inside the quotes: \" \\ \n are escapes)
; Lines starting with ; or // or # are comments.
; Keep the %d %u %s %.1f ... placeholders exactly as in English (same order and type),
; otherwise the translation of that line is ignored and the built-in English text is used.
; Select the language in zipmax.ini:  language = <file name without .lng>   (or  language = auto)
; Keys that start with IDC_ or are IDOK/IDCANCEL are the texts of buttons and labels of the dialogs.

