IDS_ABOUT_TEXT = "ZipMax Reborn is a modern version of ZipMax 0.51 (originally by Roman Scherzer, 2002-2005). It keeps everything ZipMax did - re-compress zip files with several packers and keep the smallest result of each file - on a modern, maintained foundation.\n\nIMPROVEMENTS (newest first)\n\nVersion 1.2.1\n- Settings > Language: choose the language of the program straight from the menu (English and Portugues (Brasil) are included; any file added to the language folder shows up in the list).\n\nVersion 1.2.0\n- Menu bar: File, Settings and About.\n- File menu: choose one file, several files or a folder (with or without subfolders) to process.\n- Settings > Options: every zipmax.ini parameter with a checkbox (and a text or a choice for those that need a value), saved to zipmax.ini.\n- Settings > Dialog Box: choose which columns and items the window shows and in which order. The original look is the default.\n- This About box.\n\nVersion 1.1.0\n- Full Unicode support (file names in any language, e.g. Japanese).\n- Language files (language folder): English and Portugues (Brasil).\n- Green total progress bar with the percentage inside.\n- New columns: Size Before, Size After and Type | Compression | Dictionary | Method.\n- More robust cleanup of the temporary folders.\n\nVersion 1.0.0\n- The ZipArchive library was replaced by 7-Zip (7z.dll or linked statically into ZipMax.exe).\n- Builds with Visual Studio 2026 (x64 and Win32).\n\nOriginal ZipMax 0.51: Copyright (C) 2002-2005 Roman Scherzer.\nZipMax Reborn uses 7-Zip, Copyright (C) Igor Pavlov (GNU LGPL)."
